batdetect binary distribution

This binary is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
(GPL-3.0.txt), because it bundles FFmpeg 7.1.1 built with --enable-gpl --enable-version3,
linked to the GPL libraries x264, x265, rubberband and vidstab. FFmpeg and these libraries
come with the opencv-python-headless wheel (LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt).

The batdetect source code is MIT-licensed (LICENSE). The source of this binary is the
tag v<version> printed by `batdetect --version`, built with mise.toml and uv.lock:
https://github.com/zaratan/chiro-dvr/tags

FFmpeg 7.1.1 sources:
https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.1.tar.xz

Homebrew formula that built this FFmpeg, with its patches (/opt/homebrew/Cellar/ffmpeg/7.1.1_3):
https://github.com/Homebrew/homebrew-core/blob/a671b0c7ae230e99a07f541b471a974e3dbfd403/Formula/f/ffmpeg.rb

Python packages:
- opencv-python-headless 5.0.0.93 (cv2), Apache-2.0, https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python/tree/93
- numpy 2.5.3, BSD-3-Clause, licenses in _internal/numpy-2.5.3.dist-info/licenses

libpython3.14.dylib: CPython 3.14.8 from python-build-standalone 20261001, PSF-2.0 (LICENSE-PYTHON.txt)
  https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases/tag/20261001
  Statically linked dependencies (OpenSSL, SQLite, libffi, expat, mpdecimal, bzip2, liblzma,
  zlib, libedit, ncurses...): license texts in python/licenses/ of
  https://github.com/astral-sh/python-build-standalone/releases/download/20261001/cpython-3.14.8%2B20261001-aarch64-apple-darwin-pgo%2Blto-full.tar.zst

Shared libraries from the opencv-python-headless wheel. They are Homebrew bottles installed
when the wheel was built (https://github.com/opencv/opencv-python/blob/93/travis_config.sh).
Each line gives the file, the Homebrew formula, its version when the library records its
build prefix (? otherwise; the file name carries the library version), the formula license,
and the formula history in homebrew-core.

